WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:08.137
Telo Ride 1 is one class on one bike. From this slice on, every screen says its

00:00:08.137 --> 00:00:09.703
name: Telo Ride 1.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:16.067
The header's lockup now reads Telo, Ride 1, with Ride 1 in signal orange. A screen

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:19.309
reader hears one image, named Telo Ride 1.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.095
It is on Connect Bike, the class, the class ride, the result, and page not found.

00:00:28.095 --> 00:00:30.679
Nothing else on those screens changed.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.069
Every title and message that names the product says Telo Ride 1, with the digit. So

00:00:41.069 --> 00:00:43.986
does the name the browser installs it under.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:52.812
The wordmark shows on every screen, from a phone to a desktop.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.664
Below 384 pixels, only the class ride drops the words and keeps the mark. The new

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:08.827
spec caught the class dropping them too, and that is fixed.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.552
Six new specs failed first: five on the old name, and one on the hidden words. Now

00:01:17.552 --> 00:01:21.526
one hundred and fifty-two specs and every unit test pass.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:30.825
Telo Ride 1, from the Telo family, is the focused edition of Telo Ride: one class,

00:01:30.825 --> 00:01:32.021
nothing else.

00:01:32.366 --> 00:01:37.318
It pairs with a smart bike at home over Bluetooth, plays the class video, or draws

00:01:37.318 --> 00:01:42.330
the Ibiza Sunset Strip course to music if the rider chooses it, and sets the bike's

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:45.831
resistance for every interval while the rider pedals.

00:01:46.176 --> 00:01:50.152
Connect the bike, take the class, see your number, and come back to beat it.
